{"name":"Haunted Forest","hex":"#032e0e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"haunted","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a location, frequented by a ghost or ghosts.","Obsessed (by an idea, threat, etc.)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of haunt"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/haunted"},{"term":"forest","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dense uncultivated tract of trees and undergrowth, larger than woods.","Any dense collection or amount."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover an area with trees."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forest"}],"entries":[{"title":"Haunted Forest (2007 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Haunted Forest is a 2007 American Horror film directed by Mauro Borrelli and starring Sevy Di Cione, Adam Green and Kiralee Hayashi. The film premiered at the Oxford International Film Festival on April 6, 2007. Shot entirely in California and Nevada, it is produced by Fotocomics Productions and released in the U.S. by Lionsgate."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haunted_Forest_(2007_film)","wikidata":"Q5682641"},{"title":"Haunted Forest (2017 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Haunted Forest is a 2017 Filipino supernatural horror film directed by Ian Loreños, and starring Jane Oineza, Maris Racal, Jameson Blake and Jon Lucas. It is the second installment in the Haunted film series, following Haunted Mansion in 2015. The film follows a teenager who moves to a rural town with her estranged policeman father, where she encounters a supernatural presence deep inside a forest."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e2/Haunted_Forest_2017_movie_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haunted_Forest_(2017_film)","wikidata":"Q48674040"},{"title":"Forest","blocks":[{"text":"A forest is an ecosystem characterized by a dense community of trees. Hundreds of definitions of forest are used throughout the world, incorporating factors such as tree density, tree height, land use, legal standing, and ecological function. The United Nations' Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO) defines a forest as, \"Land spanning more than 0.5 hectares with trees higher than 5 meters and a canopy cover of more than 10 percent, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ. It does not include land that is predominantly under agricultural or urban use.\" Using this definition, Global Forest Resources Assessment 2025 found that forests covered 4.14 billion hectares, or approximately 31 percent of the world's land area in 2025."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Aerial_view_of_the_Amazon_Rainforest.jpg/330px-Aerial_view_of_the_Amazon_Rainforest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forest","wikidata":"Q4421"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Adirondacks_2016_Cascade_mountain_hike.jpg/500px-Adirondacks_2016_Cascade_mountain_hike.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Adirondacks_2016_Cascade_mountain_hike.jpg/1280px-Adirondacks_2016_Cascade_mountain_hike.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Adirondacks_2016_Cascade_mountain_hike.jpg/500px-Adirondacks_2016_Cascade_mountain_hike.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The heavily traversed Adirondack Mountains of Upstate New York form the southernmost part of the Eastern forest-boreal transition ecoregion, constituting part of the world's taiga biome.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAdirondacks_2016_Cascade_mountain_hike.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/t